Subject: Cantor Identity Accounting Journal and Host Protocol P1 Justification

& [Decision]
  + append-only snapshots plus semantically replayed patches are selected because a root hash alone can detect bytes changing but cannot explain or reconstruct the identity transition
  + canonical caller-storable bytes are selected because durability needs a stable boundary without granting the semantic core ambient filesystem authority
  + one strict operation union is selected because inference should request projection resolution inspection and mutation through inspectable typed intentions
  + read operations return no successor because observation must not silently become state change
  + exact journal ledger and object compare-and-set bindings are all retained because each closes a different stale-context race

& [Rejected]
  + event records containing only before and after hashes because they cannot semantically replay the transition
  + fuzzy identity selection for mutation because similarity is not objective identity
  + hidden automatic persistence because it introduces ambient effects and unverifiable host state
  + history truncation because it destroys the accounting basis P1 exists to provide
